title: POD claims ndjson can return undef; _decode_stream always returns an ArrayRef
updated: 2026-08-27T06:36:15Z
---

Four POD blocks promise a return value the transport cannot produce.

  API::Docker::API::Plugins/install:  'or C<undef> when the engine sent no
                                       progress at all'
  API::Docker::API::Plugins/upgrade:  same sentence
  API::Docker::API::Plugins/push:     same sentence
  API::Docker::API::Images/load:      'Should an engine answer a quiet load
                                       with a body of no bytes at all, the
                                       transport returns undef rather than an
                                       empty ArrayRef, so a caller that
                                       iterates the result unconditionally
                                       must guard for it.'

Role::HTTP::_request with ndjson => 1 calls _decode_stream, which returns
\@events -- an ArrayRef, empty when the body carried nothing. The empty-body
check that returns undef sits *after* the ndjson branch, and its own comment
says so: 'ndjson promises an ArrayRef of events even for a stream carrying a
single object, so a stream that carried none is []'.

So the guard those four blocks tell a caller to write is for a case that
cannot happen. Fix: say [] in all four places. No code change.

Found while wiring the streaming callbacks (#21); left alone there to keep
that change to one subject.
